  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1000 PM CST Fri Nov 13 2026\n\nPersistence forecast of dry weather continues for the better part\nof the next week as upper ridge builds and surface high dominates\nthe eastern CONUS. Next chances for light precip then look to \narrive on Thursday as low pressure skirts the US/Canada border and\ntrailing cold front tracks through the upper Mississippi Valley.\nDominant precip type should be rain due to temperatures reading\nmainly in the 50s. However, potential for measurable precip this \nfar out in the forecast period remains uncertain due to influence \nof high pressure/dry airmass in vicinity. More widespread precip \nchances associated with organized low pressure don't look to \narrive until the end of the work week.\n\nFollowing a brief period of near average temperatures, gradual\nwarming trend then sets in at the beginning of the work week as \nsoutherly/return flow takes hold. When all is said and done, \nhighs will once again be flirting with 60 degrees in/around the \nFox Valley by the end of next week. Ensembles show a tight 25th to\n75th percentile spread during this time, lending to a high \nconfidence forecast for above average temperatures.",
